Tools and Technologies

The following tools were used during the practical excercise-

1. John the Ripper (JTR)

A password security auditing tool used to test password hashes against possible password candidates.

2. Networkwalks Hash Calculator

Used to generate password hashes from input text.

3. Networkwalks Password Cracker

Used to perform password-cracking exercises on generated hashes.

These tools provided practical exposure to password hashing and the process of evaluating password strength.
